      "message": "Here is what happened in `305d592de7` and why squishing caused the text to overlap the action buttons on mobile:\n\n1. **History of `305d592de7`**: That change moved `line-break: anywhere;` from the mobile media query into `.headerSubject` globally (for long unbroken tokens in subjects), and also added `whitespace: no-wrap; overflow: auto;`. Because `whitespace: no-wrap` was a CSS typo, browsers ignored it at the time and titles continued wrapping. Later, `996de26f23` fixed the `lit-analyzer` warning by changing `whitespace: no-wrap` to valid `white-space: nowrap`, which activated `nowrap` and made `line-break: anywhere` right above it dead code.\n2. **Why mobile overflows \u0026 why squishing overlaps `Submit`**: In `@media screen and (max-width: 50em)` (lines 1115–1129), `.header` switches to `flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start;`, but `.headerTitle` still inherits `flex: 1` (`flex: 1 1 0%`) from the desktop rule. In a column flex container, `flex-basis: 0%` applies to the **vertical** height (causing wrapped/squished content to overlap `.commitActions` below it), while `align-items: flex-start` leaves the horizontal width unconstrained without `max-width: 100%` / `width: 100%`.\n\nDepending on which behavior we prefer on mobile:\n- **To keep the copy button on the same line as the title** (without overlapping the buttons below): in `@media screen and (max-width: 50em)`, set `flex: initial; width: 100%; flex-wrap: nowrap;` on `.headerTitle` and `min-width: 0; flex: 1;` on `.headerSubject`.\n- **Or to allow wrapping**: remove `white-space: nowrap; overflow: auto;` from `.headerSubject` (so `line-break: anywhere;` works again) and set `flex: initial; max-width: 100%;` on `.headerTitle` in the mobile media query.",
